from base import *
F='team-file'
R('REQ-001','Registry files and their shape','PH-11',['CFG-TEAMS','DEF-ENTRY'],
 'Team entries live in `<home>/teams.json` as `{"schema":"backlog-teams/2","teams":{...}}` and behaviour definitions in `<home>/workflows.json` as `{"schema":"backlog-workflows/2","workflows":{...}}`; the shapes are `schema/teams.schema.json` and `schema/workflows.schema.json`.',
 'A version key needs a wrapper object; two files keep names apart from behaviour (D-02).',
 ['`team define` and `team workflow --file` write exactly these shapes (2-space JSON, trailing newline), committed and pushed as today.','A reader given a file of that shape with valid content runs; any other top-level key is `not a key of this object`.'],
 [('team define writes the schema 2 teams file','Given a repository with a backlog\n  And the backlog registers the workflow "team" from the template "team.full.json"\n  And the team configuration is a committed file\nWhen I define the team from the JSON `{"schema":"backlog-team-definition/2","name":"gold","workflow":"team","lead":"ann","members":["bob","cy"]}`\nThen the command succeeds\n  And the file "teams.json" of the backlog home has the JSON value "backlog-teams/2" at "schema"\n  And the file "teams.json" of the backlog home has the JSON value "ann" at "teams.gold.lead"'),
  ('team workflow writes the schema 2 workflows file','Given a repository with a backlog\nWhen I run `backlog team workflow --file <template:team.full.json>`\nThen the command succeeds\n  And the file "workflows.json" of the backlog home has the JSON value "backlog-workflows/2" at "schema"')],
 [('engine-files.test.js','writes teams.json as {schema, teams}','define input gold','file equals the expected JSON'),('engine-files.test.js','writes workflows.json as {schema, workflows}','team.full.json','file equals the expected JSON'),('engine-files.test.js','rejects an unknown top-level key','teams.json with extra key','error "teams.json: extra: not a key of this object"')],F)
R('REQ-002','Schema identity and version check','PH-11',['ST-LEGACY'],
 'Every reader checks the `schema` value first. A schema-1 file (no `schema` key, or a definition with `version: 1`) stops the command with `❌ backlog: <home>/<file> is schema 1; run backlog team migrate` (exit 2); an unknown schema value is a structural error.',
 'No backwards compatibility: migrate or fail with a clear message.',
 ['The message names the file and the command.','Nothing is written.','A schema 2 file is accepted.'],
 [('a schema 1 teams file stops every team command','Given a repository with a backlog\n  And the file "teams.json" of the backlog home is `{"t1":{"lead":"lead","members":["ann"]}}`\nWhen I run `backlog team query --team t1 --agent ann --claimable`\nThen the command fails with exit code 2\n  And the output contains "teams.json is schema 1; run backlog team migrate"'),
  ('a schema 1 workflow stops team commands','Given a repository with a backlog\n  And the file "workflows.json" of the backlog home is `{"team":{"workflow":"team","version":1}}`\n  And the file "teams.json" of the backlog home is `{"schema":"backlog-teams/2","teams":{"t1":{"workflow":"team","lead":"lead","members":["ann"]}}}`\nWhen I run `backlog team pop --team t1 --agent ann --dry-run`\nThen the command fails with exit code 2\n  And the output contains "workflows.json is schema 1; run backlog team migrate"')],
 [('engine-files.test.js','detects schema 1 teams.json (flat map)','teams-v1.json','throws exit 2 with the migrate text'),('engine-files.test.js','detects schema 1 workflow (version 1)','workflows-v1.json','throws exit 2 with the migrate text'),('engine-files.test.js','accepts schema 2','teams.example.json','no error')],F)
R('REQ-003','Discovery: only the backlog home, no shipped fallback','PH-11',['CFG-WORKFLOW-LOAD','SHIP-TEAMCACHE'],
 'The enforcer reads `<home>/teams.json` and `<home>/workflows.json` and nothing else: no `templates/` file, no environment variable, no other folder. A team entry naming an unregistered workflow is error E-01.',
 'The team behaviour is controlled outside the CLI (principle, D-01).',
 ['Deleting `templates/team-behaviour/` from the package changes no command result.','An entry with `workflow: team` and no registered `team` fails E-01 even though the template exists.'],
 [('an unregistered workflow is not taken from the CLI package','Given a repository with a backlog\n  And the file "workflows.json" of the backlog home is `{"schema":"backlog-workflows/2","workflows":{}}`\n  And the file "teams.json" of the backlog home is `{"schema":"backlog-teams/2","teams":{"t1":{"workflow":"team","lead":"lead","members":["ann"]}}}`\nWhen I run `backlog team query --team t1 --agent ann --claimable`\nThen the command fails with exit code 2\n  And the output contains "teams.t1.workflow: team is not registered in workflows.json"')],
 [('engine-files.test.js','never reads templates at run time','package without templates/team-behaviour','results equal'),('user-guard.test.js','no run-time import of templates/team-behaviour','source scan','no match outside tests and migrate'),('engine-files.test.js','E-01 unregistered workflow','teams.example.json without workflows','error text E-01')],F)
R('REQ-004','Validate once per process, then cache','PH-0',['ST-VALIDATE','DEF-TEAM'],
 'On first use in a process the enforcer parses both registries, runs the structural interpreter (REQ-012) and the semantic rules (REQ-013) over the whole files, and caches the result; later reads in the process use the cache. A write by `team define`/`team workflow`/`team migrate` invalidates the cache.',
 'Validation errors must surface before any evaluation; repeated parsing is waste.',
 ['A file with any error makes the first team command fail (REQ-006) even when the failing key belongs to another team.','Two reads in one process parse the file once (spy).'],
 [('a broken entry of another team still stops the command','Given a repository with a backlog\n  And the backlog registers the workflow "team" from the template "team.full.json"\n  And the file "teams.json" of the backlog home is `{"schema":"backlog-teams/2","teams":{"t1":{"workflow":"team","lead":"lead","members":["ann"]},"t2":{"workflow":"team","lead":"x","members":[]}}}`\nWhen I run `backlog team query --team t1 --agent ann --claimable`\nThen the command fails with exit code 2\n  And the output contains "teams.t2.members: must have at least 1 entries"')],
 [('engine-files.test.js','parses each registry once per process','spy on readFileSync','1 read each'),('engine-files.test.js','cache is dropped after a registry write','define then read','second read sees the new entry')],F)
R('REQ-005','Missing files and unknown teams','PH-11',['DEF-NOTCONF','CFG-TEAMS'],
 'A missing `teams.json` means no team is configured: a team command prints the fixed text `❌ team <team> is not configured in the backlog configuration` (stdout, exit 1). A missing `workflows.json` with an entry in `teams.json` is E-01 (exit 2). A user command never reads them for unbound items.',
 'Missing configuration is a normal state of a backlog without teams; a team with an entry but no behaviour is a broken configuration.',
 ['Exit codes and texts as stated.','A backlog with no team files runs every user command unchanged.'],
 [('a team without an entry is refused','Given a repository with a backlog\nWhen I run `backlog team query --team nobody --agent ann --claimable`\nThen the command fails with exit code 1\n  And the output contains "team nobody is not configured in the backlog configuration"'),
  ('user commands do not need team files','Given a repository with a backlog\n  And an item "User" exists\nWhen I run `backlog update 1 --name "User 2"`\nThen the command succeeds')],
 [('engine-files.test.js','missing teams.json: team not configured (exit 1)','empty home','stdout text, exit 1'),('engine-files.test.js','missing workflows.json with entries: E-01','teams only','exit 2')],F)
R('REQ-006','Invalid files fail closed','PH-11',['CFG-TEAMS-SILENT','CFG-WORKFLOW-LOAD'],
 'Unreadable, non-JSON or invalid registry files stop every team command and every user command that meets a bound item: `❌ backlog: <file>: invalid team configuration (<n> problem(s)); run backlog team validate` followed by the first problem line (stderr, exit 2); nothing is written.',
 'Today such files are read as empty (F7): a silent default the principle rules out.',
 ['No write, no commit.','User commands on unbound items are unaffected.'],
 [('a non-JSON teams file stops a team command','Given a repository with a backlog\n  And the file "teams.json" of the backlog home is `{not json`\nWhen I run `backlog team pop --team t1 --agent ann --dry-run`\nThen the command fails with exit code 2\n  And the output contains "invalid team configuration"'),
  ('a user command on a bound item fails closed with a broken file','Given a repository with a backlog\n  And an item "Bound" exists\n  And item 1 has the front-matter fields `{"team":"t1","status":"new"}`\n  And the file "teams.json" of the backlog home is `{not json`\n  And I take a snapshot of the backlog repository\nWhen I run `backlog update 1 --name x`\nThen the command fails with exit code 2\n  And the backlog repository is unchanged since the snapshot')],
 [('engine-files.test.js','non-JSON registry: exit 2, first problem printed','broken file','text and code'),('engine-binding.test.js','port fails closed on invalid files for bound items','broken file + bound item','exit 2, no write'),('engine-binding.test.js','port ignores invalid files for unbound items','broken file + user items','allow')],F)
R('REQ-007','backlog team validate','PH-0',['ST-VALIDATE','DEF-TEAM'],
 '`backlog team validate` validates the registered `teams.json` and `workflows.json` (both, all entries). Valid: `✅ teams.json, workflows.json: valid (<t> teams, <w> workflows)` (stdout, exit 0). Invalid: one `❌ backlog: <file>: <problem>` line per problem on stderr, exit 2. `--json`: `{"ok":true|false,"files":[{"file":"teams.json","errors":[...]},{"file":"workflows.json","errors":[...]}]}` on stdout, exit 0 or 2. It needs no `--team`/`--agent`. Help: `backlog team validate --help` prints the usage, the two files, the exit codes and one example.',
 'The owner asked for a validation command; it is the place where an operator learns every problem at once.',
 ['All problems are listed, sorted by file then path.','A schema 1 file prints the migrate message as its problem.','Help text test.'],
 [('validate reports every problem','Given a repository with a backlog\n  And the backlog registers the workflow "team" from the template "team.full.json"\n  And the file "teams.json" of the backlog home is `{"schema":"backlog-teams/2","teams":{"t1":{"workflow":"team","lead":"","members":[]}}}`\nWhen I run `backlog team validate`\nThen the command fails with exit code 2\n  And the output contains "teams.json: teams.t1.lead: must match"\n  And the output contains "teams.json: teams.t1.members: must have at least 1 entries"'),
  ('validate passes a valid configuration',BG_TEAM+'\nWhen I run `backlog team validate`\nThen the command succeeds\n  And the output contains "valid (1 teams, 1 workflows)"'),
  ('validate --json',BG_TEAM+'\nWhen I run `backlog team validate --json`\nThen the command succeeds\n  And the output contains "\\"ok\\": true"')],
 [('team-validate-cli.test.js','valid configuration: exit 0 and the counts','teams.example.json + both templates','stdout line'),('team-validate-cli.test.js','every problem one line, sorted','fixture with 3 errors','3 lines, exit 2'),('team-validate-cli.test.js','--json shape','valid and invalid','JSON shape'),('team-validate-cli.test.js','--help names files, exit codes, example','-','help text')],F)
R('REQ-008','backlog team validate --file','PH-0',['ST-VALIDATE','DEF-TEAM'],
 '`backlog team validate --file <path>` validates one input file before registration: by its `schema` value a behaviour definition (`backlog-team-behaviour/2`) or a team definition (`backlog-team-definition/2`; its workflow must be registered); any other or missing `schema`: `❌ backlog: <path>: schema must be backlog-team-behaviour/2 or backlog-team-definition/2` exit 2. Output and exit codes as REQ-007 (`✅ <path>: valid`).',
 'A definition is written outside the CLI and must be checkable before it is published.',
 ['Works without network and writes nothing.','Unreadable file: `❌ backlog: cannot read <path>: <code>` exit 2.'],
 [('a definition file with an unknown status is refused','Given a repository with a backlog\n  And a definition file "def.json" from the template "team.full.json" with `initial = "draft"`\nWhen I run `backlog team validate --file def.json`\nThen the command fails with exit code 2\n  And the output contains "def.json: initial: draft is not one of statuses"'),
  ('the templates are valid','Given a repository with a backlog\n  And a definition file "def.json" from the template "minimal.json" with ``\nWhen I run `backlog team validate --file def.json`\nThen the command succeeds')],
 [('team-validate-cli.test.js','--file selects the schema by its schema key','both kinds','valid'),('team-validate-cli.test.js','--file with unknown schema','{"schema":"x"}','exit 2 text'),('team-validate-cli.test.js','--file unreadable','missing path','exit 2 text')],F)
R('REQ-009','Registration of a behaviour definition','PH-0',['DEF-WFREG','ST-VALIDATE','DI-DEFINE-IO'],
 '`backlog team workflow --file <path>` registers a valid schema 2 definition under its `workflow` name (validation as REQ-008; problems as REQ-007 lines, exit 2, nothing written); `--show <name>` prints the registered definition (2-space JSON) or `❌ backlog: workflow <name> is not registered (backlog team workflow --file <json> registers one)` exit 2 — it never shows a template.',
 'Registration is the only way a behaviour enters a backlog (D-01).',
 ['Re-registering identical content prints `workflow <name> unchanged`.','In use by open items: the existing refusal (DI-DEFINE-INUSE).'],
 [('a valid definition is registered','Given a repository with a backlog\nWhen I run `backlog team workflow --file <template:minimal.json>`\nThen the command succeeds\n  And the output contains "workflow minimal registered"'),
  ('--show never falls back to the package','Given a repository with a backlog\nWhen I run `backlog team workflow --show team`\nThen the command fails with exit code 2\n  And the output contains "workflow team is not registered"')],
 [('team-validate-cli.test.js','workflow --file registers schema 2 only','v1 and v2 files','v1 refused with migrate text'),('team-validate-cli.test.js','workflow --show unregistered','-','exit 2 text')],F)
R('REQ-010','team define validates against the referenced workflow','PH-0',['DEF-TEAM','DEF-ENTRY','DI-DEFINE-IO'],
 '`backlog team define --file <path>` accepts a `backlog-team-definition/2` file, validates it (schema + E-01..E-08 against the registered workflow) and writes the entry without `schema`/`name`, filling `review` from the workflow `defaults.review` when absent; `refinement_review`, `limits`, `chunk_scope` are accepted (F4 closed).',
 'The entry shape must be the documented one and complete.',
 ['Output unchanged: `✅ team <name> defined: lead <lead>, <n> members, flow <workflow>`.','A missing `workflow` is `missing key workflow`.'],
 [('refinement_review is definable','Given a repository with a backlog\n  And the backlog registers the workflow "team" from the template "team.full.json"\n  And the team configuration is a committed file\nWhen I define the team from the JSON `{"schema":"backlog-team-definition/2","name":"gold","workflow":"team","lead":"ann","members":["bob"],"refinement_review":[{"team":"gold","count":1}]}`\nThen the command succeeds\n  And the file "teams.json" of the backlog home has the JSON value "gold" at "teams.gold.refinement_review.0.team"'),
  ('a team definition without workflow is refused','Given a repository with a backlog\n  And the team configuration is a committed file\nWhen I define the team from the JSON `{"schema":"backlog-team-definition/2","name":"gold","lead":"ann","members":["bob"]}`\nThen the command fails with exit code 2\n  And the output contains "missing key workflow"')],
 [('team-validate-cli.test.js','define fills review from defaults.review','gold without review','entry review = defaults'),('team-validate-cli.test.js','define accepts refinement_review, limits, chunk_scope','gold full','entry has the keys'),('team-validate-cli.test.js','define E-rules','E-02..E-08 fixtures','each text')],F)
R('REQ-011','backlog team migrate','PH-11',['ST-LEGACY','RF-LEGACYSTAGE','RF-JOIN','CFG-WIPFILE','CFG-SCOPEFILE'],
 '`backlog team migrate` (no team or agent needed) converts a backlog once, in one commit `team migrate: schema 2`: (1) `teams.json` flat map → `{schema, teams}`, each entry gains `workflow` (`team` when absent), loses `wip`, gains `limits` from `<home>/wip-limits.json` (overall/repository/branch/team copied; `agent` → `member`) and `chunk_scope` from the `backlog.scope` of the folders of the backlog (D-14); `wip-limits.json` is deleted; (2) `workflows.json` → `{schema, workflows}`, every schema 1 definition converted by the rules of `06-migration-plan.md` §4, and the template `team.json` registered as `team` when an entry names `team` and none is registered; (3) every item of the home bound to a team with an old word (`pending`, `in_progress`, `done`, or `stage`/`review_state` keys) gets the word `statusOf` gives today, `stage`/`review_state` are removed, and a teamless split slice (body marker) whose parent is bound gets the parent\'s team; (4) the result is validated (REQ-007) before the commit; any problem aborts with the problem lines and writes nothing. `--file <path>` converts one schema 1 definition file in place (used for the topology copy, D-12). `--dry-run` prints the changes. Exit 0 / 2. Already schema 2: `ℹ️  nothing to migrate` exit 0.',
 'No backwards compatibility: every reader drops its translation; the data is changed once.',
 ['Idempotent.','Unbound items are never changed (user words are free).','Two backlog.scope values for one team: abort listing the folders.'],
 [('migrate converts a schema 1 backlog','Given a repository with a backlog\n  And the file "teams.json" of the backlog home is `{"t1":{"lead":"lead","members":["ann"],"wip":{"agent":1,"team":4}}}`\n  And an item "Old" exists\n  And item 1 has the front-matter fields `{"team":"t1","status":"pending","stage":"ready"}`\nWhen I run `backlog team migrate`\nThen the command succeeds\n  And the file "teams.json" of the backlog home has the JSON value "team" at "teams.t1.workflow"\n  And item 1 has status "ready"\n  And item 1 has stage ""'),
  ('migrate is idempotent',BG_TEAM+'\nWhen I run `backlog team migrate`\nThen the command succeeds\n  And the output contains "nothing to migrate"'),
  ('migrate leaves unbound items alone','Given a repository with a backlog\n  And the file "teams.json" of the backlog home is `{"t1":{"lead":"lead","members":["ann"]}}`\n  And an item "User" exists\n  And I run `backlog update 1 --status in_progress`\nWhen I run `backlog team migrate`\nThen the command succeeds\n  And item 1 has status "in_progress"')],
 [('team-migrate.test.js','teams.json flat → schema 2 with workflow team','teams-v1.json','expected file'),('team-migrate.test.js','wip-limits.json → entry limits, file deleted','wip fixture','limits copied, agent→member'),('team-migrate.test.js','backlog.scope → chunk_scope; conflict aborts','two folders','abort text'),('team-migrate.test.js','item words translated like statusOf (table of 14 cases)','legacy items','each word'),('team-migrate.test.js','teamless split slice gets the parent team','slice fixture','team set'),('team-migrate.test.js','--file converts the example-team definition','backlog-workflow.json copy','valid schema 2'),('team-migrate.test.js','--dry-run writes nothing','v1 home','no change'),('team-migrate.test.js','invalid result aborts, nothing written','entry with bad lead','exit 2')],'team-migrate')
R('REQ-012','JSON Schema subset interpreter','PH-0',['ST-VALIDATE','DEF-TEAM'],
 'The schema files are JSON Schema 2020-12 using only: `type`, `const`, `enum`, `anyOf`, `required`, `properties`, `additionalProperties` (false or schema), `propertyNames`, `minProperties`, `items`, `minItems`, `uniqueItems`, `pattern`, `minLength`, `minimum`, `$ref` (local `#/$defs/...` and the `$id` of a sibling schema), `$defs`, `$id`, `$schema`, `title`. The interpreter `src/engine/schema.js` implements exactly these with the messages of §4; a schema using another keyword fails a test.',
 'Zero runtime dependencies (D-04); one interpreter for all files.',
 ['The reference implementation `tools/validate_subset.py` and the JS module give the same problem list on the fixture corpus.'],
 [('the shipped schemas use only the subset','Given a repository with a backlog\nWhen I run `backlog team validate --file <template:team.full.json>`\nThen the command succeeds')],
 [('engine-schema.test.js','each keyword: one passing and one failing case with the exact message','keyword table','messages of §4'),('engine-schema.test.js','schema files use no other keyword','schema/*.json','no unknown keyword'),('engine-schema.test.js','same problems as the reference interpreter','corpus of 40 invalid definitions','equal lists')],F)
R('REQ-013','Semantic validation rules','PH-0',['ST-VALIDATE','DEF-TEAM'],
 'After the structural pass the validator applies V-01..V-30 (definitions) and E-01..E-08 (entries) with the texts of §4 and §5; every rule is one function with a test that triggers it once.',
 'Cross-references (a status used in a step, a role used in `by`) cannot be expressed in the schema subset.',
 ['Each rule has one Examples row in `features/validator-keys.feature`.'],
 [('every semantic rule triggers with its text','See the Scenario Outline in features/validator-keys.feature')],
 [('engine-validate.test.js','V-01..V-30 each: fixture triggers exactly that text','team.full.json patched','one problem'),('engine-validate.test.js','E-01..E-08 each','teams.example.json patched','one problem')],'validator-keys')
R('REQ-014','Shipped templates','PH-0',['SHIP-TEAMCACHE','ST-VOCAB'],
 'The package ships `templates/team-behaviour/team.json` (= this plan\'s `templates/team.full.json`), `minimal.json`, `teams.example.json`, and the four schema files under `templates/team-behaviour/schema/`. Each template is valid; `team.json` reproduces today\'s team (§9, REQ-907). Templates are documentation and the input of `team workflow --file`/`team migrate`, never read at run time (REQ-003).',
 'A documented starting point per use: a full team, a minimal team.',
 ['`backlog team validate --file` passes each template.','The README names them.'],
 [('the full template validates','Given a repository with a backlog\nWhen I run `backlog team validate --file <template:team.full.json>`\nThen the command succeeds'),('the minimal template validates','Given a repository with a backlog\nWhen I run `backlog team validate --file <template:minimal.json>`\nThen the command succeeds')],
 [('engine-conformance.test.js','templates validate','templates/*','valid'),('package.test.js','package files include templates/team-behaviour','npm pack list','present')],F)
R('REQ-015','Redefinition of a team or workflow in use','-',['DI-DEFINE-INUSE'],
 'Unchanged machinery: `team define` refuses a changed entry of a team with open items, `team workflow --file` a changed definition used by teams with open items (texts as today), exit 2.',
 'In-flight items keep the definition they started with (DATA-INTEGRITY).',
 ['Existing tests stay green.'],
 [('a team with open items is not redefined',BG_TEAM+'\n  And the team configuration is a committed file\n  And I act as agent "lead"\n  And I run `backlog team new --team t1 --name "Open" --objective o --summary s`\nWhen I define the team from the JSON `{"schema":"backlog-team-definition/2","name":"t1","workflow":"team","lead":"lead","members":["ann"]}`\nThen the command fails with exit code 2\n  And the output contains "has 1 open items; register the new composition under another name"')],
 [('team-cli.test.js','define refuses a team in use (kept)','existing','unchanged')],F)
